      "created_at": "2014-10-03T16:38:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We've all seen the threads about Savage Mana and Ammo Drop, but I would like to start a discussion about Savage Mana and Savage Mana.</p><p>Savage Mana put targets Haka destroys under Savage Mana.</p><p>Savage Mana destroys the targets under it.</p><p>Targets he destroys are put under Savage Mana.</p><p>Shouldn't he be allowed (forced?) to put the targets destroyed from beneath Savage Mana directly back under Savage Mana since those targets are destroyed (by Savage Mana)? How is this not an infinte loop? Is it because it doesn't specifically say that <em><strong>Haka </strong></em>destroys the targets under it?&nbsp; Is there a precedent for treating a character's Ongoing cards with Powers as separate from themselves?<br>If that's the case, are there any messed up situations caused by this in either Haka or other characters not being properly attributed damage or destruction?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:36.662Z",
